<section id="about" class="home-manifesto">
	<h2 id="manifesto-heading">
		I design ideas and build the websites they live on.   Some ideas spark
		something in me
		<span class="accent"> instantly.</span>
		When it hits, I follow it all the way — research, iteration, obsessing over
		details — until it becomes a product people <span class="accent">
			will</span
		> actually use.
	</h2>

	<div class="home-split">
		<div class="home-split-left">
			<p>
				I’m a people person at heart, so I design for humans first and
				users second. Humans aren’t rational robots: we make mistakes,
				change our minds and love things with character. That’s why I
				leave room for personality and a bit of human chaos in my work.
				Because design isn’t about being perfect, it’s just thinking
				made visual.
			</p>
			<p>
				In an age dominated by AI, reminding ourselves of our
				humanity—and that you don't need to be perfect to be
				authentic—is everything to stand out.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
